    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67077" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετεκ-βαίνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go from one into another</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετεκβαίνεσκε</span> (
				Ion.
			
			impf.) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ ἅρματος ἐς ἁρμάμαξαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.41
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				100
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς πλοῖον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					5.21
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in speaking,
				<i>pass on</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. εἰς ἕτερόν τινα λόγον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					642b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				935a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. acc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. φθόγγον</span>
			<i>pass from one</i> note <i>to another,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				12.187
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Strat.
			</span></i>).</div>
